  <exercise number="325" has_solution="true">
    <problem>
      <p>Given $$x = f(t)$$ and $$y = g(t),$$ if $$\frac{dx}{dy} = \frac{dy}{dx},$$ then $$f(t) = g(t) + \text{C,}$$ where C is a constant.</p>
